Task: Fix Docker Buildx Bake Multi-Service Build File

Context & Overview:
Your team uses Docker Buildx Bake to build container images for a multi-service application (frontend, backend, database) in parallel using a declarative HCL configuration file (docker-bake.hcl).

Currently, running "docker buildx bake" fails due to configuration errors and target mismatches in docker-bake.hcl.

Your objective is to fix docker-bake.hcl so all services build cleanly and are tagged under the "hire-spec/" image namespace.

Task Requirements:
1. Fix target name references in docker-bake.hcl so "group default" correctly builds all three services: frontend, backend, and database.
2. Ensure each target context points to its respective directory (./frontend, ./backend, ./database).
3. Update image tags for all services to use the "hire-spec/" repository namespace:
   - frontend target  -> hire-spec/frontend:latest
   - backend target   -> hire-spec/backend:latest
   - database target  -> hire-spec/database:latest
4. Ensure running "docker buildx bake --load" completes without errors and loads all three images into Docker.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Running "docker buildx bake --load" exits with status 0.
- All three Docker images exist in the local Docker daemon:
  - hire-spec/frontend:latest
  - hire-spec/backend:latest
  - hire-spec/database:latest

Local Verification Commands:
1. Execute Buildx Bake to build and load all images:
   docker buildx bake --load

2. Check built images:
   docker images | grep hire-spec
